  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>Milo is a small Piscataquis County town of approximately 2,300 residents on the Sebec River, between Dover-Foxcroft (15 min north) and Howland/Bangor (40 min south). The town has one cannabis dispensary — GreenLife Recreational Dispensary, opened April 13, 2023, owned and operated by Bob Ade.</p>
    <p>Milo is part of the broader Piscataquis County cannabis corridor. Per the <a href="/guides/dover-foxcroft-dispensary-guide">Dover-Foxcroft guide</a>, the Dover-Foxcroft dispensary count is currently "uncertain" as of mid-2026 after the primary-source spot-check retracted an earlier claim of "Dab Bar operating since 2020" (the dabbars.org source is now a parked GoDaddy placeholder). For the surrounding rural communities — Sebec, Atkinson, Brownville, LaGrange, and Howland — Milo's GreenLife is the closest confirmed adult-use option.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>GreenLife Recreational Dispensary</h2>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 19 Park Street, Milo, ME 04463<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 943-9005 (per Piscataquis Chamber of Commerce listing)<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Adult-use / Recreational (21+ with valid ID)<br>
    <strong>Rating:</strong> 4.9★ from 60+ Google reviews per public directory listings</p>
    <p>GreenLife opened with a grand opening and ribbon cutting on April 13, 2023 per the Piscataquis Observer's coverage of the launch. The facility is owned and operated by Bob Ade, who was named the Piscataquis Chamber's 2022 Business of the Year recipient for his Pat's Pizza franchise locations in Dover-Foxcroft and Milo.</p>
    <p>Bob Ade's GreenLife dispensary is part of a broader entrepreneurial footprint in the region — Ade runs the Pat's Pizza franchises in Dover-Foxcroft and Milo, and the GreenLife dispensary extends that local-business presence into the cannabis market. The combination gives Ade a recognizable community-business identity that other dispensaries in the area lack.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The Piscataquis County Cannabis Corridor</h2>
    <p>Milo is the southern anchor of Piscataquis County's small cannabis market. The county's two dispensary locations are:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Milo (this guide):</strong> GreenLife Recreational Dispensary — opened April 2023 per the Piscataquis Observer. Adult-use.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For Piscataquis County residents, GreenLife Milo is the most reliably-verified adult-use storefront in the area; the Dover-Foxcroft status is currently "uncertain" per the spot-check on that guide. For the broader central Maine interior — Howland, Lagrange, Brownville, Sebec, Atkinson, Sangerville, Guilford — the corridor serves a substantial rural population with limited access to adult-use retail.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Service Area</h2>
    <p>GreenLife Milo serves the central Maine interior south of Dover-Foxcroft:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Milo</strong> (in town) — 5 min</li>
      <li><strong>Sebec</strong> — 10 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Atkinson</strong> — 15 min south</li>
      <li><strong>Brownville</strong> — 15 min east</li>
      <li><strong>LaGrange</strong> — 20 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Howland</strong> — 25 min south</li>
      <li><strong>Dover-Foxcroft</strong> — 15 min north (other Piscataquis County dispensary)</li>
      <li><strong>Bangor</strong> — 45 min south</li>
      <li><strong>Millinocket</strong> — 60 min northeast</li>
      <li><strong>Greenville / Moosehead Lake</strong> — 75 min north</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For Piscataquis residents, GreenLife Milo is the most reliably-verified dispensary in the area; the Dover-Foxcroft status is currently "uncertain" per the spot-check on that guide. For Penobscot County customers east of Howland, GreenLife is closer than the Bangor dispensaries.</p>
  </section>

